WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:08.760
The next operator, identity, determines if two&nbsp;
variables share the same memory location. We will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:14.520
cover this operator type and its purpose in more&nbsp;
detail later in this domain, but for this example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:21.680
look at some teams assigned to a game with their&nbsp;
color and ranks. In this 135-identity file,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:33.920
Team 2, on line 2, has been made to be a&nbsp;
clone of Team 1, on line 1. Team 3, on line 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:43.960
has the same specs as Team 1. But is Team 3 the&nbsp;
same as Team 1? The is keyword is used to identify&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:51.160
whether two variables share the same memory space.&nbsp;
On lines 5 and 6, we have two print statements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:56.080
one to see whether team 1 and team 2 share the&nbsp;
same memory space and one to see whether team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:02.920
1 and team 3 share the same memory space. Do you&nbsp;
have any guesses as to what we will see when we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:15.120
run this code? The first statement is True because&nbsp;
team 2 has been made equal to team 1. Thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:21.480
the two variables share the same memory&nbsp;
space. But, team 3, even though it looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:31.440
to be the same as team 1, is technically&nbsp;
a new variable with its own set of values,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:38.160
so it does not share the same memory space as&nbsp;
team 1. Later, we will see why this is important,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.720
but because we are focused on the sequence&nbsp;
of operator types compared to one another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:49.360
know that identity happens before logical and&nbsp;
assignment but after arithmetic and comparison.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.360
The importance of identity in this context is&nbsp;
that if two variables share the same memory space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.280
they will have equal values, and thus,&nbsp;
a developer can decide which variable to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:03.920
change later in code, if necessary,&nbsp;
to help fulfill the goal of an app.

